---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../../site.config';

/**
 * L'elenco dei cookie deve restare fedele a ciò che il sito fa davvero:
 * il consenso non è più gestito da un banner nostro, ma da Cloudflare
 * Zaraz (piattaforma di consent management della zona tuscanytrail.it):
 * è Zaraz a decidere se e quando caricare Google Analytics 4, e a
 * ricordare la scelta della visitatrice. Se cambia la configurazione
 * Zaraz, cambia questa pagina.
 */
const lastUpdated = 'September 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Cookie policy — Tuscany Trail 365"
  description="Which cookies this site sets, when, and how to change your mind."
>
  <div class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="kick">Legal</div>
      <h1>Cookie policy</h1>
      <p class="lead">Short version: nothing is set until you say yes.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:760px">
      <p class="small">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <h2 class="sec">We set no cookies of our own</h2>
      <p>
        This site stores nothing on your device to make its own pages work.
        There is no login, no shopping cart and no session to remember, so
        there are no technical cookies to tell you about.
      </p>
      <p>
        The consent banner you see is not ours: it is run by Cloudflare
        Zaraz, the consent management platform for the whole
        tuscanytrail.it domain. Zaraz remembers your answer on your device
        and decides whether Google Analytics is allowed to load — we never
        see or store that choice ourselves.
      </p>

      <h2 class="sec" style="margin-top:34px">Analytics cookies — only after you accept</h2>
      <p>
        If you press <em>Accept</em>, Google Analytics 4 sets these cookies:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <code>_ga</code> — distinguishes one visitor from another. Expires
          after 2 years.
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>_ga_FELFB9W37W</code> — keeps the state of the current visit for
          this site's analytics property. Expires after 2 years.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Cloudflare Zaraz keeps Google Analytics in a denied, cookieless state
        by default and only lets it start writing once you accept. Ad
        storage, ad user data and ad personalisation stay denied whatever you
        choose: we do not advertise and we do not build profiles.
      </p>
      <p>
        One honest caveat about <code>_ga</code>. This site lives at
        <code>365.tuscanytrail.it</code>, and Google Analytics
        writes that cookie for the whole of <code>tuscanytrail.it</code> — so if
        you have already visited the Tuscany Trail website, your browser is
        carrying a <code>_ga</code> cookie before you ever reach us. We neither
        set it nor read it until you accept. What is unambiguously ours is
        <code>_ga_FELFB9W37W</code>, and that one appears only after you press
        <em>Accept</em>.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you press <em>Decline</em>, we write no analytics cookie at all.
      </p>

      <h2 class="sec" style="margin-top:34px">Changing your mind</h2>
      <p>
        Use the <a href="/cookie-policy/" data-cookie-prefs>Cookie preferences</a>
        link in the footer of every page to reopen the consent choice at any
        time. You can also clear the site data for this domain in your
        browser, which removes any analytics cookie and makes the banner
        greet you again on your next visit. In most browsers this lives
        under Settings → Privacy → Cookies and site data, or in the padlock
        menu in the address bar.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can also refuse cookies browser-wide, or install Google's
        <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Analytics opt-out add-on</a>.
        Nothing on this site depends on cookies, so refusing them costs you no
        functionality at all.
      </p>

      <h2 class="sec" style="margin-top:34px">Sites we link to, and maps we show</h2>
      <p>
        The accommodation and route buttons take you to Stay22, to the
        properties' own websites and to Ride with GPS. Those are other people's
        sites with their own cookies and their own policies — this page only
        covers what happens here. See the
        <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> for how those
        links work.
      </p>
      <p>
        Two maps are shown inside our own pages rather than linked. The booking
        map comes from Stay22, and the trail map of the Monte Calvi bike area
        comes from Trailforks. They load from those companies' servers and can
        set their own cookies on their own domains as soon as the map appears,
        which is outside our consent banner and outside our control. Neither map
        is needed to read the page, and blocking third-party cookies in your
        browser leaves the rest of the site working exactly as before.
      </p>

      <p style="margin-top:34px">
        Questions about any of this? Write to
        <a href={`mailto:${site.brand.email}`}>{site.brand.email}</a>. How we
        handle personal data more generally is in the
        <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
